WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.089
<v Examiner>Four marks.

2
00:00:02.089 --> 00:00:04.622
<v Examiner>Define the social determinants of health.

3
00:00:04.622 --> 00:00:09.069
<v Examiner>Then identify two determinants, and explain how each one affects health.

4
00:00:09.519 --> 00:00:12.631
Three command words: define, identify, explain.

5
00:00:12.631 --> 00:00:18.393
So roughly one mark for the definition, one for naming two, and two for the explaining.

6
00:00:18.393 --> 00:00:22.632
Lisa said it plainly on the twenty-seventh: always give the why.

7
00:00:22.632 --> 00:00:26.009
Education is linked to better health is not enough.

8
00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:28.396
The definition, in her words.

9
00:00:28.396 --> 00:00:34.407
The social determinants of health are the conditions in which people are born, grow, work,

10
00:00:34.407 --> 00:00:40.418
live and age: the wider set of forces and systems that shape the conditions of daily life.

11
00:00:40.418 --> 00:00:42.354
There's no single fixed list.

12
00:00:42.354 --> 00:00:44.358
It changes as society changes.

13
00:00:44.808 --> 00:00:48.065
Determinant one: the social gradient, which is income.

14
00:00:48.065 --> 00:00:50.718
The lower a person's socioeconomic position,

15
00:00:50.718 --> 00:00:54.397
the worse their health and the shorter their life expectancy,

16
00:00:54.397 --> 00:00:56.629
even after you account for behaviour.

17
00:00:56.629 --> 00:01:01.634
Income is the most powerful determinant: poverty means less money for healthy food,

18
00:01:01.634 --> 00:01:03.987
warm housing and getting to the doctor,

19
00:01:03.987 --> 00:01:07.123
and the stress of money trouble itself harms health.

20
00:01:07.573 --> 00:01:09.126
Determinant two: stress.

21
00:01:09.126 --> 00:01:12.299
Chronic stress keeps the body in fight or flight.

22
00:01:12.299 --> 00:01:16.895
Over time that damages the cardiovascular system and the immune system,

23
00:01:16.895 --> 00:01:18.773
and it affects mental health.

24
00:01:19.223 --> 00:01:23.743
If you'd rather pick others, here are her eleven, each with its why.

25
00:01:23.743 --> 00:01:29.060
Work: a stable income helps, but unemployment means less security and stability.

26
00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:33.181
Education: better jobs, critical thinking and health literacy.

27
00:01:33.181 --> 00:01:38.166
Early life: childhood trauma and stress lead to mental illness and obesity,

28
00:01:38.166 --> 00:01:41.157
then heart disease and type 2 diabetes later.

29
00:01:41.157 --> 00:01:46.408
Social exclusion: discrimination by ethnicity, gender, age or rainbow identity,

30
00:01:46.408 --> 00:01:52.258
mostly in the workplace, limits work and can lead to homelessness and the poverty cycle.

31
00:01:52.258 --> 00:01:57.110
The health system itself: how accessible, affordable and available it is.

32
00:01:57.110 --> 00:02:01.098
Transport: access to services, pollution, and active travel.

33
00:02:01.098 --> 00:02:05.485
Conflict: it disrupts how resources and medicines are distributed.

34
00:02:05.485 --> 00:02:09.008
Food security: what's cheap is not always nutritious,

35
00:02:09.008 --> 00:02:11.999
and you can be malnourished while overweight.

36
00:02:11.999 --> 00:02:15.854
And addiction: tobacco, alcohol, drugs, gambling and food,

37
00:02:15.854 --> 00:02:18.845
which affect relationships and mental health.

38
00:02:19.295 --> 00:02:25.366
Social determinants: the conditions in which people are born, grow, work, live and age.

39
00:02:25.366 --> 00:02:27.320
Name one, then give its why.

40
00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:32.414
Income and the social gradient: lower status, worse health, shorter life.

41
00:02:32.414 --> 00:02:37.718
Stress: chronic fight or flight harms the heart, immunity and mental health.

42
00:02:37.718 --> 00:02:40.579
Education: jobs, income, health literacy.

43
00:02:40.579 --> 00:02:44.905
Early life: childhood trauma leads to mental illness, obesity,

44
00:02:44.905 --> 00:02:47.208
later heart disease and diabetes.
